; ===========================================================================
; Bonded parameters for the GB1 position-53 guest set, completed 2026-10-04.
;
; ATB, QFL and HFL were shipped as rtp entries without their bonded terms, so
; a morph whose hybrid actually used them failed in gentop/grompp:
;     Error B: No bond entry found for bstate CA-CB (CT1-CG311 -> CT1-CG311)
;     ERROR: No default U-B types for interaction  (CT1-CG321-CG302)
; ATB is the sharpest case: Abu has only a two-carbon side chain, so its CF3
; sits one bond closer to the backbone than in QFL/HFL/TFLE and creates a
; CT1-CG321-CG302 junction no other fluoro residue produces.
;
; Every line below is copied VERBATIM, with its original provenance comment,
; from the CGenFF 5.0 distribution (charmm36-feb2026_cgenff-5.0.ff/ffbonded.itp).
; Nothing here is an analogy or a fitted guess.  Selection rule: every atom type
; in the term is one used by ALA/GLY/ABA/LEU/PHE/ATB/QFL/HFL/PF5 or by the
; protein backbone they attach to, and core did not already carry the term.
; ===========================================================================

